## [ENT-060] | 2026-11-16 19:31 UTC | Mercury | error | ref: game/routes/voidborn-neural-matrix-delivery.json | see: requests.log ENT-155
Class: a pilot taken by hand on the lock alone while the engine still runs its loop (the lock of division.py releases when the runner's order file goes, a moment before the engine's mining loop stops).
Case: 2026-11-16 19:01:52 UTC my poller held the test pilot of Neural Matrix Delivery as its gather run ended; route_run.py started at once and ended at stop 1 with 'A loop is running on this account. Stop it first.' (0/4 stops, 0 cr). The dispatcher gave the pilot its next 45-minute gather run at 19:02:53 UTC, so the test waits about an hour.
Effect: no credits lost; the 5,000 cr test moved to after 19:48 UTC.
Cause: my poller asked only division.py may; the pilot's live file still showed activity kind loop. mine.py waits up to 40 x 15 s for an earlier goal before it starts its loop; route_run.py does not.
Fix, done: the poller (scripts/catch.py of my skill trade-books) skips a pilot whose live file shows a loop, and the skill says so; the test itself is now a route in the plan (voidborn-neural-matrix-delivery, requires.stored), which the dispatcher starts when the gather run has ended.
Would it have prevented this one: yes; at 19:01:52 the live file read activity kind loop.

## [ENT-061] | 2026-11-16 19:58 UTC | Apophis | error | ref: game/routes/guidebook/military.md | see: queue.log ENT-115
Class: a shared file left modified in the clone while I waited for a result (the rule of rulebook section 10: build in scratch, copy in and commit in one step).
